<title>USA: No damaging cold seen in Brazil coffee areas - WSC.</title>
<headline>No damaging cold seen in Brazil coffee areas - WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>No damaging cold is seen in Brazil's coffee regions after late-weekend chilly weather that brought low temperatures of 39-47F in the south and 47-57 in the north and on the coast, independent forecaster Weather Services Corporation (WSC) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Lows of 37-45F are expected on Monday morning, followed by lows of 39-50 on Tuesday morning.</p>
<p>The outlook is for moderating temperatures from Wednesday to Friday, with no damaging cold likely through the end of the week.</p>
</text>
